---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import type { CasePart } from "../types";
import apparatus from "./driving-apparatus.png";
import roadworks from "./driving-roadworks.jpeg";
import pedestrians from "./driving-pedestrian.jpeg";

interface Props {
  part: CasePart;
}

const { part } = Astro.props;
---

{part === "intro" && (
  <p>
    In this independent project, I designed the experiment, extended{" "}
    <a href="https://github.com/Westdrive-Workgroup/LoopAR-public">LoopAR</a> in
    Unity and C#, and analyzed behavioral and physiological records.
  </p>
)}

{part === "visual" && (
  <figure class="portfolio-figure driving-apparatus">
    <Image
      src={apparatus}
      alt="Research setup with a seated person wearing a VR headset and using a steering wheel and pedals, with recording leads attached."
      format="webp"
      widths={[360, 520, apparatus.width]}
      sizes="(min-width: 720px) 657px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
      width={apparatus.width}
      height={apparatus.height}
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <figcaption>
      The experiment combined a VR headset, steering wheel and pedals with
      physiological recording.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{part === "body" && (
  <>
    <section aria-labelledby="driving-preparation-heading">
      <h2 id="driving-preparation-heading">Preparing to take control</h2>
      <p>
        Taking control involves more than a first response. This study separated
        the opportunity to inspect the road from the actions that followed,
        asking how prior driving tendencies and preparation related to the
        transition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before the takeover trials, manual-driving observations characterized
        participants&apos; slowing and steering; questionnaire items about
        cautious driving provided a separate source of prior information.
      </p>

      <figure
        class="portfolio-diagram driving-sequence"
        aria-labelledby="driving-sequence-heading"
        aria-describedby="driving-sequence-caption"
      >
        <h3 id="driving-sequence-heading">
          From preparation to manual control
        </h3>
        <p class="portfolio-note driving-prior">
          <strong>Before the trials</strong>
          <span>Manual-driving observations</span>
        </p>

        <ol class="driving-stages" role="list" aria-label="Trial stages">
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage">
            <h4>Automated driving</h4>
            <p>
              Assigned participant groups: one-back or three-back letter-memory
              task, or control.
            </p>
            <p class="driving-record">Responses in memory-task groups</p>
          </li>
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage">
            <h4>Observe the road</h4>
            <p>
              A monitoring request prompts road viewing. Automation retains
              control.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage">
            <h4>Situation-awareness questions</h4>
            <p>Road hidden; simulation paused.</p>
            <p class="driving-record">Question responses</p>
          </li>
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage driving-transfer">
            <h4>Transfer to manual control</h4>
            <ol class="driving-handover" aria-label="Control transfer steps">
              <li>Scene resumes</li>
              <li>Takeover request</li>
              <li>Manual control</li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage">
            <h4>Drive through the event</h4>
            <p>Steering, pedal input and speed recorded.</p>
            <p class="driving-record">Driving inputs</p>
          </li>
          <li class="portfolio-node driving-stage">
            <h4>Workload ratings</h4>
            <p>Ratings after the driving event.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="driving-continuous">
          Cardiac (ECG), muscle (EMG) and electrodermal (EDA) activity were
          recorded throughout the trial.
        </p>
        <figcaption id="driving-sequence-caption">
          The trial separates road observation, a paused situation-awareness
          probe, and the transfer to manual control. This is a conceptual
          sequence; spacing does not represent duration.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        To probe what participants had noticed before taking control, I paused
        the simulated world and hid the road during the questions. Participants
        answered without further road viewing, while the question timer ran
        independently of simulation time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="driving-recording-heading">
      <h2 id="driving-recording-heading">Recording the transition</h2>
      <p>
        I implemented event markers and timestamped driving records so task and
        control transitions could be matched across recordings. Steering, pedal
        input and speed were recorded alongside event information, and I added
        an interface for sending markers to physiological acquisition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Roadworks and pedestrians provided two simulated contexts for the
        takeover tasks.
      </p>
      <div class="driving-scenarios">
        <figure class="portfolio-figure">
          <Image
            src={roadworks}
            alt="Simulated road with traffic cones and construction equipment ahead."
            format="webp"
            widths={[320, roadworks.width]}
            sizes="(min-width: 640px) 336px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
            width={roadworks.width}
            height={roadworks.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>Roadworks scenario overview</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="portfolio-figure">
          <Image
            src={pedestrians}
            alt="Two pedestrian figures ahead on a simulated road."
            format="webp"
            widths={[320, pedestrians.width]}
            sizes="(min-width: 640px) 336px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
            width={pedestrians.width}
            height={pedestrians.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>Pedestrian scenario overview</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="portfolio-note driving-source">
        Equipment and scenario images from the study materials.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="driving-analysis-heading">
      <h2 id="driving-analysis-heading">Analyzing action sequences</h2>
      <p>
        I examined initial braking and steering, then the sequence of actions
        after manual control was transferred to the driver. Across the analyses,
        I related these records to prior-driving observations, responses to the
        situation-awareness questions and physiological measures, accounting for
        repeated observations within drivers.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project shaped my interest in how assistance can support preparation
        before a demanding action, and how that support may differ across
        people.
      </p>
    </section>
  </>
)}

<style>
  .driving-apparatus {
    width: min(100%, 657px);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .driving-apparatus :global(img),
  .driving-scenarios :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .driving-sequence h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
  }

  .driving-prior {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.15rem 0.75rem;
    padding: 0 0 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
  }

  .driving-stages {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    gap: 0.9rem;
    counter-reset: driving-stage;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .driving-stage {
    position: relative;
    counter-increment: driving-stage;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1rem 1rem 3rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .driving-stage::before {
    content: counter(driving-stage);
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.95rem;
    left: 1rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .driving-stage h4 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
  }

  .driving-stage p {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
  }

  .driving-stage .driving-record {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--portfolio-line);
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .driving-handover {
    list-style-type: lower-alpha;
    margin: 0.55rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--portfolio-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .driving-handover li {
    margin: 0.15rem 0;
    padding-left: 0.2rem;
  }

  .driving-handover li::marker {
    color: var(--portfolio-accent);
  }

  .driving-continuous {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--portfolio-accent);
    background: var(--portfolio-surface);
    color: var(--portfolio-ink);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .driving-scenarios {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    align-items: start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .driving-scenarios figure {
    margin: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .driving-scenarios figure:first-child {
    max-width: 523px;
  }

  .driving-scenarios figure:last-child {
    max-width: 507px;
  }

  .driving-source {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 539px) {
    .driving-stage {
      padding: min(1rem, 16px) min(1rem, 16px) min(1rem, 16px) min(3rem, 48px);
    }

    .driving-stage::before {
      top: min(0.95rem, 16px);
      left: min(1rem, 16px);
    }

    .driving-handover {
      padding-left: min(1.15rem, 24px);
    }

    .driving-handover li {
      padding-left: min(0.2rem, 4px);
    }

    .driving-continuous {
      padding-inline: min(1rem, 16px);
    }
  }
</style>
